    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1665">

                <pb facs="1060" n="944" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg944"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.51/621a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Brown Brothers &amp; Company
                        and Seligman &amp; Company.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-01-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 13, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: The Nicaraguan Minister has
                    represented to the Department that the economic conditions now existing in his
                    country render it desirable that the Nicaraguan Government increase its <pb
                        facs="1061" n="945" xml:id="pg945"/> present loan by $250,000, or perhaps as
                    much as $500,000. The Department will be glad to assist in forwarding any
                    practical measure calculated to relieve the financial conditions now obtaining
                    in Nicaragua. Should you care at this time to consider an increase in your loan
                    to the Government of Nicaragua, the Department will be glad to discuss the
                    matter with your representatives at such time as may best suit your
                    convenience.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
